# Chaos: soft glow (bloom) on bright light only (O210; src/framework/core/graphicalapplication.h/.cpp, graphics/painter.h/.cpp,
# luafunctions.cpp, and Lua: mods/client_settings/classes/dataset.lua, options/graphics.otui; after 0001-0131). Owner overlay
# module game_visualfx (client/MANIFEST.md "Visual effects") owns the option and the shaders. The owner's rule: the biome's own
# colours stay; only what is already bright gets a halo.
#  * g_app.setMapBloom(enabled, strength) / g_app.isMapBloom(): GraphicalApplication::drawMapBloom runs on the graphics thread
#    right after the map picture is drawn to the screen (both render loops). Off (the default) = one atomic read, no buffers.
#    On: the map framebuffer source rect is drawn at 1/4 size into bloom buffer A with the shader chaos_bloom_extract (only a
#    luma above 0.80, smooth to 0.96, passes; everything else is black), blurred A -> B -> A by chaos_bloom_blur (one horizontal
#    and one vertical pass, 5 bilinear taps each), and A is drawn once over the map rect at the strength with the new
#    Painter::CompositionMode_Screen (src + dst * (1 - src)). Black adds nothing, white cannot get whiter, so no pixel far from a
#    bright one changes and the picture is never washed out; only dark pixels next to a bright one pick up the halo.
#  * The two shaders are created by game_visualfx (data/shaders/chaos_bloom_*.frag); a missing shader skips the glow.
#  * dataset.lua: option `bloom` (default off); options/graphics.otui: an eighth checkbox "Soft glow" under "Rain and weather"
#    (the panel grows from 143 to 162 px).
# Cost in client/BASE.md. Checked: applies cleanly after 0001-0131 (no fuzz); the touched .cpp files pass g++ -fsyntax-only (the
# only errors are the base's own g_app / g_atlas declarations of a build without the framework defines); not run in a client.
